[statement]
A pax `size` record overrides the header's size, whatever the header says.
Here the record says zero and the header declares a body holding two headers,
which every reader then lists as members, and so does ferrotape.

[archive]
pax size=0
header name=outer size=1024
header name=smuggled1
header name=smuggled2
header name=tail
data "hello\n"
end

[verdict]
all: read

[gnu-tar 1.35]
member listed=- path=outer size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
member listed=- path=smuggled1 size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
member listed=- path=smuggled2 size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
member listed=- path=tail size=6 mode=0o644 data="hello\n"
exit 0

